@L 2026_06_12_lane2_h1182 := "Lane 2 rung-2 SHIPPED — H_1182 🔴 critical-capacity scaling law REFUTED + bimodality discovery" :: log [active]
  result = "H_1182 CLOSED-NEGATIVE ($0): K* does NOT scale with #regimes. K*_by_regime={3:12,4:24,6:32,8:32,10:4}, Spearman(N,K*)=0.0, cells/regime CoV=0.49. The H_1178 '~5.3 cells/regime' was a 6-regime coincidence (32/6), not a law"
  serendip = "Lane-2 payoff (only visible reading the full d-curves, not the scalar test): the d(deriv,metro) curve is BIMODAL. (A) a mid-capacity peak at a roughly ABSOLUTE K~=24-32 INDEPENDENT of N (substrate DIM=8/T=2400-set, not per-regime) + (B) an emergent LOW-capacity scarcity peak at K=4 that WINS at high N (N=10 d=+1.24 global max — scarce cells placed by event beat the blind clock, a distinct mechanism). argmax flips between A and B as N grows = what breaks the scaling"
  finding = "the critical capacity is substrate-ABSOLUTE + bimodal, NOT complexity-proportional. H_1178 stands (its N=6 K*=32 reproduced exactly) but its location is not a per-regime budget; the 5.3 reading was special to N=6 where peak A dominated"
  honest = "toy AUDIO DIM=8/T=2400, coarse quantized cap ladder; the absolute ~24-32 is itself substrate-specific (a_scale_honest_scope). h1159b refuted as the K*-location explanation. live CORE + real-model unverified"
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1182_critical_capacity_scaling.py · .verdicts/1182_critical_capacity_scaling/H_1182.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE/discoveries/1182_critical_capacity_scaling.tape (NEW per-domain convention)"
  next = "Lane 2: the bimodality opens a cleaner rung — separate the two mechanisms (scarcity-placement vs coverage-completion) on a fixed N with a fine cap ladder; or promote the absolute-K* reading by varying DIM/T. Lane 1 open-rung list depleted (H_1179-1181 terminal)"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1183 := "Lane 2 rung-3 SHIPPED — H_1183 🟢 BIMODAL confirmed (H_1182 serendip validated, not coarse aliasing)" :: log [active]
  result = "H_1183 SUPPORTED ($0): fine cap ladder at fixed N=10 shows the d(deriv,metro) stage-decode curve is genuinely BIMODAL — peaks K=4 (+1.24) and K=40 (+1.29), valley_min=-0.236 (K5-16 dead zone). F1+F2 pass. Not coarse-ladder aliasing"
  finding = "TWO distinct event-driven advantage regimes: (A) low-K scarcity-placement (K=4: event places too-few cells at change-points, beats blind clock) + (B) mid/high coverage-completion (broad ridge K=20-64, peak K=40). Dead valley between. Sharpens H_1178's single inverted-U (= coverage ridge alone) into a two-regime structure; vindicates H_1182 serendip"
  honest = "toy AUDIO N=10 DIM=8/T=2400 10 seeds; peak POSITIONS substrate-specific (a_scale_honest_scope), the two-regime STRUCTURE + placement-vs-coverage mechanism split is the transferable claim. live CORE + real-model unverified"
  convention = "first discovery written under the NEW convention — appended into domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md (### h1183_bimodal_capacity tape block), NOT a discoveries/ subfolder (a_discovery_log)"
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1183_bimodal_capacity.py · .verdicts/1183_bimodal_capacity/H_1183.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1183_bimodal_capacity"
  next = "tick/capacity discovery arc has a clean 3-rung result (H_1178 asymmetric inverted-U -> H_1182 scaling refuted+bimodal serendip -> H_1183 bimodal confirmed). Candidate /paper at FULL closure (a_paper_only_at_closure); or pivot Lane 2 to a fresh axis"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1184 := "Lane 2 rung-4 SHIPPED — H_1184 🔴 closed-neg-with-SPLIT: the two bimodal peaks are OPPOSITE on temporality" :: log [active]
  result = "H_1184 CLOSED-NEG on joint claim (F1 pass F2 fail) but the per-peak split IS the finding. K=40 coverage: d_real=+1.29 d_shuf=+0.22 (shuffle KILLS = temporal). K=4 scarcity: d_real=+1.24 d_shuf=+2.67 (shuffle IMPROVES = NOT temporal)"
  discovery = "Lane-2 payoff + H_1183 correction: the two H_1183 advantage peaks are NOT two sizes of one mechanism — they are mechanistically OPPOSITE on the temporality axis. coverage peak (mid-K) = genuine event/time-driven (contrasts the temporally-blind H_1179/1180); scarcity peak (low-K) = NON-temporal variance-spread sampler (shuffle helps it). H_1183's 'precise temporal placement' label for K=4 is CORRECTED to distribution-spreading"
  finding = "temporal-grounding is the knife that separates the bimodality: only the coverage peak reads time. New axis (temporality) pursued from the Lane-1 thread paid off — the event-tick's genuinely temporal half is isolated"
  honest = "toy AUDIO N=10 10 seeds; shuffle isolates temporal ORDER (dist + (X,stage) pairing preserved). dichotomy transfers, exact d's substrate-specific (a_scale_honest_scope). live CORE + real-model unverified"
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1184_temporal_grounding.py · .verdicts/1184_temporal_grounding/H_1184.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1184_temporal_grounding"
  next = "tick arc now 4 rungs (1178 asymmetric-U -> 1182 scaling-refuted+bimodal -> 1183 bimodal-confirmed -> 1184 temporal-split). The coverage peak = the publishable temporal mechanism. Candidate /paper at closure"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1185 := "Lane 2 rung-5 SHIPPED — H_1185 🔴 the temporal coverage mechanism is AUDIO-specific / capacity-ratio gated, not modality-portable" :: log [active]
  result = "H_1185 CLOSED-NEG: re-running the H_1184 shuffle test on TEXT at K{4,40} — K=4 non-temporal signature carries over (drop -0.41), but K=40 has NO coverage peak (d_real=-0.30, derivative WORSE than metronome). The temporal coverage mechanism does not appear on text at the audio-borrowed caps"
  finding = "the genuine temporal half of the bimodality (coverage peak) is GATED by capacity-to-regime ratio, not freely modality-portable. text(4 stages)/K=40 = ~10 cells/stage over-provision -> coverage edge vanishes+inverts. consistent with H_1182 (absolute ~24-32 coverage capacity) + H_1183 (regimes-vs-cells balance). the K=4 variance-spread non-temporal signature IS modality-general"
  honest = "HONEST pre-reg limitation (a_completeness_over_cheap, no goalpost move): caps {4,40} borrowed from audio's 10-regime peak, not re-derived for 4-stage text, so K=40 is out-of-band. fair test needs text's own coverage cap. toy $0"
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1185_temporal_grounding_text.py · .verdicts/1185_temporal_grounding_text/H_1185.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1185_temporal_grounding_text"
  next = "tick arc 5 rungs (1178->1182->1183->1184->1185). substrate showing diminishing returns at fixed audio caps; a fair modality test would re-derive text's coverage cap (bigger rung). candidate /paper at closure; or pivot Lane 2 to a fresh substrate/axis"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1186 := "Lane 2 rung-6 SHIPPED — H_1186 🔴 per-modality temporal ranking: video=most time-dependent, audio=most profitable, text=non-temporal" :: log [active]
  result = "H_1186 (fixes H_1185 by finding each stream's OWN cap): audio K*32 d_real+1.15 drop+0.88 TEMPORAL; video K*64 d_real+0.49 d_shuf-0.62 drop+1.11 (most time-dependent but d_real 0.49 just under 0.5 bar -> strict 🔴); text K*4 drop-0.41 non-temporal"
  discovery = "two orthogonal rankings split: TEMPORAL-DEPENDENCE (shuffle drop) video>audio>text; ORDERED-ADVANTAGE audio>video~text. video is most temporally FRAGILE (derivative becomes WORSE than metronome when time scrambled, d_shuf-0.62) yet modest ordered advantage (far-apart scenes easy for both). audio = goldilocks (big + time-dependent)"
  reading = "'how do we read?' = surprise-driven saccades = the event tick. but TOY byte-text shows no temporal peak even at own cap -> needs REAL text + a LEARNED surprise model; saccadic-reading unconfirmable on toy byte features (honest). mechanism-analogy stands as a hypothesis for a learned-surprise re-test"
  honest = "toy video = smooth-motion+cuts (not real frames); 0.5 bar frozen not moved (video misses honestly). per-stream own-cap fixes H_1185 flaw. real modalities + learned encoders unverified (a_scale_honest_scope)"
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1186_temporal_grounding_modalities.py · .verdicts/1186_temporal_grounding_modalities/H_1186.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1186_temporal_grounding_modalities"
  next = "tick arc 6 rungs. clean next: a LEARNED-surprise text reader (next-token-predictability gate) to test the saccadic-reading hypothesis properly — but that needs a trained predictor (bigger rung). candidate /paper at closure"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1189 := "H_1189 🔴 CLOSED-NEG — SIMULTANEOUS (동시) TEXT+AUDIO+IMAGE fusion does NOT help super-additively; H_1170 surface-gating confirmed even with perfect time-alignment" :: log [active]
  lane = "Lane-2 MITOSIS-ENGINE · temporality arc (H_1184-1186) × cross-modal super-additivity arc (H_1167-1170) · $0 CPU 10-seed · p7/g5 · FROZEN pre-reg · answers user '텍스트 + 오디오 + 이미지, 동시도, 실험'"
  method = "ONE shared scene timeline stage[t] drives 3 DIM-8 sub-vectors (audio drift-tone / text byte-feature / image static-spatial); FUSED = concat 24-d → DIM=8 fixed seeded projection. reuse h1163 grow_arm/stage_decode VERBATIM; per-stream K*=argmax d(DERIVATIVE,METRONOME) over {4..64}; derivative decode acc @ K*; time-shuffle @ K*."
  falsifier = "FROZEN: F1 SUPER-ADDITIVE d(FUSED − best-single)>=0.5; F2 TEMPORAL fused drop=d_real−d_shuf>=0.5. SUPPORTED iff F1 and F2."
  verdict = "CLOSED-NEGATIVE. F2 PASS (fused K*=12 d_real=+1.28 d_shuf=−0.43 drop=+1.72 — fused advantage IS temporal). F1 FAIL HARD: fused acc=0.349 vs best-single(image)=0.837, Δ=−0.488, d=−2.79 (fusion WORSE than best part). per-stream: audio K*32 acc0.595 / text K*32 acc0.615 / image K*24 acc0.827 / FUSED K*12 acc0.349 (chance0.167)."
  discovery = "동시(same-tick) fusion does NOT manufacture super-additivity — it DESTROYS decode by MIXING three distinct geometries through the 24→8 projection: the cleanest single modality (image static-per-scene, acc0.83) is best, fusion blends it down to 0.349 (below every single). DIRECTLY confirms H_1170 surface-gating — the 3 share only the abstract regime LABEL, not preserved per-modality surface, so even PERFECT time-alignment buys no super-additive whole. 1+1+1 < best(1). Fused advantage is temporal (F2) but temporality without surface-preserved alignment buys nothing — H_1170's shared-surface requirement is the binding constraint even for 동시 input."
  honest = "TOY ($0, 10 seeds) synthetic modalities (NOT real TTS/images/learned encoders, cf H_1170). DIMENSIONALITY: grow_arm/stage_decode hardcoded to DIM=8 → all streams DIM=8; fused 24-d PROJECTED (not widened) via fixed seeded random projection. label-aligned only (the H_1170 gate), projection = partial mixing surface-bridge. frozen bars not moved. live CORE + real modalities + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope)."
  refs = "h1170 (surface-gated cross-modal surplus — confirmed) · h1167-h1169 · h1184-h1186 (temporality arc) · h1163 (substrate reused) · h1155 · a_completeness_over_cheap · a_scale_honest_scope · a_paper_negative_ok · p7 · p8"
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1189_simultaneous_multimodal.py · .verdicts/1189_simultaneous_multimodal/H_1189.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1189_simultaneous_multimodal"
@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1188 := "Lane 2 rung-7 SHIPPED — H_1188 🟢 SUPPORTED: numeric + image join the temporal ranking; smooth within-regime APPROACH is what makes a modality temporal" :: log [active]
  result = "H_1188 (extends H_1186 ranking, own-cap K*=argmax d(DERIV,METRO), shuffle at K*): NUMERIC (per-regime AR(1)) K*16 d_real+3.17 d_shuf-0.18 drop+3.35 TEMPORAL=True (predicted YES ✓); IMAGE (static-per-scene DIM=8 frame) K*4 d_real+0.00 d_shuf+1.38 drop-1.38 TEMPORAL=False (predicted NO ✓). BOTH frozen predictions borne out. anchor AUDIO re-run reproduced H_1186 EXACTLY (K*32 d_real+1.152 drop+0.883) = harness validated"
  discovery = "FULL 5-MODALITY ranking. temporal-DEPENDENCE (shuffle drop): NUMERIC+3.35 > VIDEO+1.11 > AUDIO+0.88 > TEXT-0.41 > IMAGE-1.38. ordered-ADVANTAGE (d_real): NUMERIC+3.17 > AUDIO+1.15 > TEXT+0.50~VIDEO+0.49 > IMAGE+0.00. STRUCTURAL LAW: SMOOTH WITHIN-REGIME APPROACH makes a modality temporal — AR(1) numeric is the new goldilocks (biggest advantage AND most time-dependent) because its no-teleport carryover relaxes smoothly to each attractor (derivative fires on that rising edge, shuffle flips d negative); IMAGE is the anti-temporal endpoint (static frames = zero derivative edge over the blind clock)"
  honest = "TOY ($0, 10 seeds, DIM=8): numeric=synthetic AR(1) NOT real sensors; image=DIM=8 flattened static frame+pixel noise NOT real images (cf H_1170). predictions FROZEN pre-measure, no tune-to-green (numeric no-teleport + image static both pre-registered). 0.5 bars = H_1186 frozen thresholds unmoved. real modalities + learned encoders + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope)"
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1188_numeric_image_modalities.py · .verdicts/1188_numeric_image_modalities/H_1188.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1188_numeric_image_modalities"
  next = "tick arc 7 rungs. structural law 'smooth approach = temporal' now spans 5 toy modalities. real-modality + learned-encoder re-test is the scale-up rung; candidate /paper at arc closure"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1187 := "Lane 2 rung-7 SHIPPED — H_1187 🟢 SUPPORTED: a LEARNED-SURPRISE reader DOES beat a uniform scan on real text AND is temporal — saccadic reading recovered" :: log [active]
  result = "H_1187 SUPPORTED (resolves the H_1186 deferral). Built a learned reader (order-4 hashed n-gram next-byte predictor, Laplace, trained on held-out first-50% corpus; surprise=−log2 P(byte|last-4)); split-gate fires on surprise>mean+σ (a saccade). At the text's own cap K*=24: d_real=+1.02 (F1>=0.5 PASS, surp_decode 0.598 vs metro 0.276, chance 0.25), d_shuf=+0.503, drop=+0.512 (F2>=0.5 PASS). guards PASS (11524 learned contexts, position-aligned, surprise spread 1.32 bits)."
  finding = "the saccadic-reading advantage H_1186's TOY BYTE-CHANGE derivative could NOT find on text (drop=−0.41, shuffle helped) is RECOVERED once the gate is a LEARNED predictability signal: −log2 P(byte|ctx) fires only where the model is genuinely surprised (informative byte = fixation), reads stage structure better than a uniform clock, and a time-shuffle destroys the edge (temporal). The decisive ingredient is the LEARNED surprise gate, not raw byte-change. Text analogue of H_1184's audio temporal-coverage mechanism."
  honest = "TOY $0 10 seeds: order-4 n-gram COUNT predictor on ONE corpus (NOT a real LLM); its loss is NEVER the verdict (p7=stage-decode). F2 passes by a thin 0.012 margin (d_shuf=+0.503 just over noise) — near-boundary temporal pass, robust under frozen seeds, honestly reported. own-cap protocol fixes H_1185 borrowed-cap flaw. NO goalpost moved (ladder/σ/refrac/falsifier pre-registered before the run). real-LLM surprise + eye-tracking + scale unverified (a_scale_honest_scope)."
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1187_learned_surprise_reader.py · .verdicts/1187_learned_surprise_reader/H_1187.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1187_learned_surprise_reader"
  next = "tick arc 7 rungs (1178->1182->1183->1184->1185->1186->1187). H_1187 is the affirmative capstone: saccadic reading works on real text with a learned gate. Candidate /paper at closure (the event-tick reads time on audio H_1184 + on text with a learned-surprise gate H_1187; toy byte-change is blind H_1186). Next rung could vary predictor order-k or test a real-LLM surprise proxy."

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_temporality_arc_synopsis := "SYNTHESIS — the 9-rung tick/temporality arc (H_1178..H_1189): event-tick reads time only under smooth within-regime approach" :: index [active]
  law = "UNIFYING LAW: the derivative/event tick's decode advantage over a blind metronome is TEMPORAL (killed by a time-shuffle) ONLY when the stream has SMOOTH WITHIN-REGIME APPROACH (continuous/differentiable flow toward each regime). Where values flow smoothly then transition, the derivative fires on a real rising-edge and shuffling destroys it; where static/jumpy, no temporal advantage."
  capacity = "the advantage is BIMODAL over cell-count (H_1178 asymmetric inverted-U K*=32; H_1182 scaling refuted; H_1183 bimodal confirmed): a low-K variance-spread peak (NON-temporal) + a mid-K coverage peak (TEMPORAL, H_1184 split). The coverage peak is substrate-absolute ~24-32, capacity/regime-ratio gated (H_1185)."
  modality = "per-modality temporal ranking at each stream's own cap (H_1186/H_1188): numeric(AR1)>audio>video temporally-dependent; image(static) + raw-byte-text NON-temporal. numeric is the goldilocks (biggest advantage + most time-dependent)."
  reading = "H_1187 🟢 SACCADIC READING: raw byte-change is temporally blind on text, but a LEARNED-surprise gate (-log2 P(byte|ctx)) beats uniform scan AND is temporal — humans read by surprise-driven saccades; the gate's CONTENT (learned predictability) is the knife, not raw change."
  fusion = "H_1189 🔴 SIMULTANEOUS multi-modal (text+audio+image 동시) fusion HURTS (1+1+1 < best single) absent shared SURFACE — confirms H_1170 surface-gating even under perfect time-alignment; temporality without surface-preserved correspondence buys no super-additive whole."
  honesty = "ALL toy ($0 CPU numpy, 10 seeds, frozen pre-reg falsifiers, a_scale_honest_scope): synthetic streams + toy n-gram reader, NOT real modalities/learned encoders. Scale-sensitive (a_toy_scale_recheck) — a less-toy validation is the next escalation."
  verdicts = ".verdicts/{1178..1189}_*/H_*.txt; discoveries domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1178..h1189; candidate /paper at full closure (a_paper_only_at_closure)."

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1190 := "H_1190 🔴 CLOSED-NEG — learned surprise is a TEXT-SPECIFIC rescue, NOT a universal gate upgrade: it never beats the raw |dX/dt| derivative on already-temporal numeric/audio" :: log [active]
  lane = "Lane-2 (MAIN hands-on / LLM-watched) · MITOSIS-ENGINE · $0 CPU numpy 10 seeds · g5/p7 · FROZEN pre-reg falsifier · a_paper_negative_ok"
  result = "tests whether the H_1187 learned-surprise gate (−log2 P(next|ctx)>mean+σ saccade, which RECOVERED a temporal text decode advantage the raw derivative could not) is GENERAL. Continuous surprise = one-step linear-predictor error ||X[t]−x̂_t||. Per-modality K*=argmax d(deriv,metro): NUMERIC K*=16 d_surp=+0.99 d_deriv=+3.17 Δ=−2.18 SURPRISE-WORSE; AUDIO K*=32 d_surp=+0.88 d_deriv=+1.15 Δ=−0.28 REDUNDANT. Learned surprise NEVER beats the raw derivative (Δ never >= +0.5) — strict frozen letter = CLOSED-NEG (not both-redundant), but in the OPPOSITE direction to a universal upgrade."
  finding = "ASYMMETRIC GATE-CONTENT LAW: learned-surprise beats raw-change ONLY where raw change is uninformative (text, H_1187). On smooth-flow already-temporal streams the raw derivative already reads the flow, so surprise is redundant (audio) or strictly worse (numeric AR(1) — the linear predictor FITS the smooth relaxation so it is NOT surprised on the very transitions the derivative edge catches). Both gates still beat the blind metronome, so the tick matters; only the LEARNED refinement is wasted. Right gate is modality-dependent: raw change for smooth-flow, learned surprise for non-smooth (text)."
  honesty = "TOY ($0 CPU, 10 seeds, DIM=8): synthetic numeric AR(1) + synthetic audio, TINY least-squares linear predictor (stronger nonlinear predictor UNVERIFIED). predictor error never the verdict (p7=stage-decode). reuses h1163 substrate + h1188 numeric stream VERBATIM; grow_arm_surprise = h1163 DERIVATIVE body with the H_1187 trigger swap. no goalpost move (the SURPRISE-WORSE bucket is an honest third outcome the binary frozen split lacked). a_scale_honest_scope · a_toy_scale_recheck · a_lane_akida_gpu_split."
  verdicts = ".verdicts/1190_surprise_gate_generality/H_1190.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1190_surprise_gate_generality · UNIVERSE/h1190_surprise_gate_generality.py · xref h1187·h1188·h1186·h1163"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1191 := "H_1191 🔴 SURFACE-PRESERVED fusion — surface-preservation is NECESSARY-BUT-NOT-SUFFICIENT for super-additivity (closes the H_1189/H_1170 loop)" :: log [active]
  result = "CLOSED-NEGATIVE. F2 PASS (label-only control reproduces H_1189: fused 0.349 < best single image 0.837, super_add d=−2.79≤0). F1 FAIL (surface-shared fusion NOT super-additive: fused 0.120 < best single image 0.593, super_add d=−5.21<0.5 — fusion hurts EVEN MORE). Construction sound: orthogonal invertible maps cond=1, cross-modality linear R²≈0.9999 (genuinely recoverable shared surface)."
  finding = "giving 3 modalities a perfectly recoverable shared surface does NOT restore fused>best-single at toy scale — the concat→fixed-random-projection FUSER itself is the bottleneck (sums 3 noise/distortion draws, blurs centroids below the cleanest single view). Refines H_1170/H_1189: surface-preservation alone insufficient; also need a non-destructive (learned/aligning) fuser. toy $0 CPU 10 seeds DIM=8, a_scale_honest_scope/a_toy_scale_recheck/a_paper_negative_ok."
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1191_surface_preserved_fusion.py · .verdicts/1191_surface_preserved_fusion/H_1191.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1191_surface_preserved_fusion"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1192 := "H_1192 🟢 the FIRST real summer-training run — a REAL TRAINED numpy-MLP reader (SGD on summer CPU) DE-TOYS the H_1187 saccadic-reading 🟢: the result SURVIVES a genuine gradient-trained predictor (NOT a count-table artifact)" :: log [active]
  lane = "Lane-2 (MAIN hands-on / LLM-watched) · MITOSIS-ENGINE · RAN ON SUMMER pool host (CPU linux, python3.12 + numpy 2.4.4) · $0 CPU 10 seeds · g5/p7 · FROZEN pre-reg falsifier (SAME bars as H_1187) · a_toy_scale_recheck"
  compute = "SUMMER — trained + evaluated on the summer pool host (/home/summer/core/anima, CPU linux). The user's 'when do we train on summer?' answered NOW: this is the first real summer training run. $0 (no GPU rent; production-GPU forge/flame a_train_flame_forge = LATER escalation, summer CPU = toy→small bridge)."
  result = "de-toys H_1187 (which used a Laplace order-4 COUNT n-gram) by TRAINING a real one-hidden-layer numpy MLP next-byte predictor (k=4 one-hot→tanh 64→softmax 256, 82,240 params; SGD lr=0.30 batch=256, 8 epochs on held-out first 50% = 108k pairs, 68.1s on summer CPU) and re-running the H_1187 saccadic-reading test VERBATIM with its surprise. TRAINED MODEL not-degenerate: val_ce 4.25→2.83 bits/byte MONOTONE descent << unigram 5.91 << uniform 8.0. F1 PASS K*=4 d_surprise_vs_metro=+1.168>=0.5 (surp 0.508 vs metro 0.000); F2 PASS d_shuf=+0.547 drop=+0.621>=0.5 (time-shuffle kills it = temporal). cap=24 (H_1187's K*) also reproduces d_real=+0.909. guards PASS pre-scoring (surprise std=2.16 bits, alignment True)."
  finding = "the H_1187 saccadic-reading 🟢 SURVIVES a de-toy to a GENUINE GRADIENT-TRAINED reader — NOT a count-table artifact. A real SGD-trained MLP surprise (val_ce 2.83 < unigram 5.91, monotone descent = real learning) reproduces BOTH gates: surprise-saccade reading beats the uniform metronome scan (F1 d=+1.17 vs H_1187 +1.02) AND is temporally grounded (F2 drop=+0.62 vs H_1187 +0.51). K* shifted 24→4 (the trained MLP's surprise is peakier so even a 2-cell budget separates the informative-byte stages where the smoother n-gram needed cap 24), but cap-24 ALSO holds (d=+0.91) — not a single-cap fluke. The de-toy STRENGTHENS the finding: a real trained reader reads-by-saccade better, with fewer cells."
  honesty = "TOY-ISH but a GENUINE TRAINED model (the de-toy over H_1187's count n-gram), NOT a production LLM. reader loss NEVER the verdict (p7 = stage-decode; loss only certifies non-degenerate). reuses h1163 grow_arm/stage_decode/cohen_d/make_text_stream + h1187 grow_arm_surprise/CAP_LADDER/time-shuffle VERBATIM — ONLY the surprise SOURCE swapped (count→MLP). frozen F1/F2 + K* argmax pre-registered = H_1187 (no goalpost move). mitosis GROWTH arm stays Lane-M gradient-free (SGD trains only the surprise predictor; a_lane_akida_gpu_split). real-LLM surprise + real reading-time + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck). 82K-param toy ckpt NOT kept/uploaded ($0, no HF)."
  verdicts = ".verdicts/1192_summer_real_reader/H_1192.txt (+ H_1192.json) · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1192_summer_real_reader · UNIVERSE/h1192_summer_real_reader.py · xref h1187·h1190·h1186·h1163·a_train_flame_forge"

@L 2026_06_13_lane2_h1193 := "H_1193 🔴 CLOSED-NEG — the saccadic-reading de-toy ladder BREAKS at the neural rung: a REAL byte-level Transformer LM (GPU-trained on summer) reproduces F1 (saccade beats metronome, d=+1.00) but FAILS F2 TEMPORAL (drop=+0.43<0.5) — the BETTER predictor's surprise is a static informativeness signal, not a temporal saccade. n-gram→MLP→Transformer does NOT de-toy to completion." :: log [active]
  lane = "Lane-2 (MAIN hands-on / LLM-watched) · MITOSIS-ENGINE · de-toy of H_1187/H_1192 · RAN ON SUMMER GPU (RTX 5070 12GB, torch 2.11.0+cu130) · $0 (no rent) · 10 seeds · g5/p7 · FROZEN pre-reg falsifier (SAME bars as H_1187/H_1192) · a_toy_scale_recheck · a_paper_negative_ok"
  compute = "summer-GPU-shared — trained + evaluated on the summer pool host GPU (RTX 5070 12GB, torch 2.11.0+cu130, CUDA). VRAM capped at 28% (set_per_process_memory_fraction 0.28) right after cuda init; peak VRAM 321 MB (well under the 3424 MB cap, never grabbed more). GPU TIME-SHARED with a live co-tenant (rbfe-prod PID 110588, ~7.2GB) — co-tenant NEVER touched and still alive after the run (a_dont_kill_live_compute). $0 (no GPU rent; summer GPU). Transformer trained in 22.8s on GPU."
  result = "de-toys H_1187 (count n-gram) + H_1192 (numpy MLP) by training a REAL small byte-level Transformer LM (vocab 256, d_model=192, 3 layers, 3 heads, block=128, 1,457,856 params; AdamW lr=3e-4 cosine, batch=48, 1500 steps on held-out first 50% = 181k pairs) and re-running the H_1187/H_1192 saccadic-reading test VERBATIM with its next-byte surprise. TRANSFORMER = the BEST predictor of the ladder: val bits/byte 8.23→2.30 << H_1192 MLP 2.83 << unigram 5.91 << uniform 8.0 (guards PASS, surprise std=1.95 bits, alignment True). F1 PASS K*=4 d_surprise_vs_metro=+1.004>=0.5 (surp 0.461 vs metro 0.000); F2 FAIL d_shuf=+0.570 drop=+0.434<0.5 (time-shuffle does NOT destroy the advantage = NOT temporal). SUPPORTED=F1∧F2=FALSE."
  finding = "the saccadic-reading GREEN does NOT de-toy to completion — it BREAKS at the genuinely-neural Transformer rung, and the break LOCATION is the finding. The n-gram (drop=+0.51) and MLP (drop=+0.62) both passed F2 TEMPORAL, but the STRONGEST predictor (a real attention Transformer, val 2.30 bits/byte) fails F2 (drop=+0.43): its saccade STILL beats the metronome on real-ordered text (F1 d=+1.00) but that edge SURVIVES a time-shuffle (d_shuf=+0.57). MECHANISM: a better next-byte model's surprise is SMOOTHER + LONGER-CONTEXT, so its high-surprise positions track DISTRIBUTIONAL informativeness (rare/hard bytes) MORE than local TEMPORAL stage-transition structure. The cruder n-gram/MLP surprise spiked SHARPLY at local context-breaks = stage edges = temporal events, so their saccade was temporal; the better model washes those local spikes into a smoother field that helps decode regardless of time-order. So saccadic-reading TEMPORALITY is a SHARPNESS artifact of weak local predictors — the better the LM, the LESS its surprise is a temporal saccade signal. An honest closed-negative that locates exactly where (F2, not F1) and why the toy greens fail to scale."
  honesty = "SMALL but GENUINELY NEURAL (1.46M-param byte Transformer, 3-layer self-attention, AdamW 1500 steps) — the strongest reader of the n-gram→MLP→Transformer ladder, NOT a production LLM. reader loss NEVER the verdict (p7 = stage-decode; val curve only certifies the model is the best non-degenerate predictor). reuses h1163 grow_arm/stage_decode/cohen_d/make_text_stream + h1187 grow_arm_surprise/CAP_LADDER/time-shuffle VERBATIM — ONLY the surprise SOURCE swapped (MLP→GPU Transformer). frozen F1/F2 + K* argmax pre-registered in the docstring = H_1187/H_1192 (no goalpost move; the F2 fail reported as-measured, a_paper_negative_ok). mitosis GROWTH arm stays Lane-M gradient-free (AdamW trains only the separate surprise predictor on Lane G GPU; a_lane_akida_gpu_split). VRAM capped 28%, peak 321 MB, co-tenant rbfe-prod untouched + alive. production-LM surprise + real human reading-time + scale UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope, a_toy_scale_recheck). 1.46M-param toy ckpt /tmp/h1193_byte_transformer.pt NOT HF-uploaded ($0, no keep)."
  verdicts = ".verdicts/1193_summer_gpu_transformer_reader/H_1193.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md ### h1193_summer_gpu_transformer_reader · UNIVERSE/h1193_summer_gpu_transformer_reader.py · xref h1192·h1187·h1190·h1186·h1163·a_paper_negative_ok·a_toy_scale_recheck"

