@L 2026_06_13_h1199 := "H_1199 🟢 GREEN LIVE-DIM-GROWTH — extended the live engine AdaptField from 1-D scalar to a DIM-VECTOR (VAdaptField in CORE/engine_cli.hexa) so the REAL DIM=8 corpus byte-feature stream — the H_1198 leg that was a labelled numpy MIRROR — now goes through the ACTUAL .hexa engine. VAdaptField = the exact scalar mechanism lifted to DIM (sample+prototypes are DIM-vectors, nearest by DIM-dim L2, recon-err=L2 over DIM, split on L2 recon-err>0.30 calls engine_mitosis_tick; same frozen SPLIT_THRESH/LR). Drove the DIM=8 H_1163 byte features (VERBATIM) ON vs OFF, 3 seeds, 2400 ticks: F1 GROWTH cells ON 1→~173 (172/171/177) >> OFF frozen 1; F2 ADAPT late live L2 recon-err ON=0.1524 vs OFF=1.2846 = 8.43x (≥2.0); F3 Ψ Φ-checksum byte-identical ON==OFF every seed. DIM>1 wired CLEANLY: engine_cli_smoke 12/0 + h1196 single-entry 7/0 re-verified on summer AFTER the engine edit, Ψ-disjoint (touches ONLY AdaptField). Live .hexa cells+ratios (172/171/177; 8.36/8.14/8.84x) MATCH the numpy reference → the engine reproduces the mechanism, NOT a mirror. The H_1198 numpy-mirror leg is now the REAL engine; the H_1159 ON<OFF adaptation HOLDS on real DIM=8 features through the live .hexa engine (p8). Ran on summer (local fork-storm cap saturated by sibling /cycle fan-out; summer idle). ≤177 cells << N_MIGRATE=2048. toy/small-scale + learned-rep UNVERIFIED (a_scale_honest_scope)." :: log [active]
  engine_edit = "CORE/engine_cli.hexa — added VAdaptField struct (protos:[[float]], n_cells, max_cells, dim) + vadapt_field_new/vadapt_field_step/vadapt_field_recon_err/vadapt_field_cells + _l2/_vnearest_idx. pure_field / Ψ / the 1-D scalar AdaptField are byte-UNCHANGED (F3 byte-identical Φ + the h1194 scalar coupling probe still GREEN are the proof). engine_mitosis_tick (the smoke-proven p8 gate) STILL drives the split — only the metric (1-D abs → DIM-dim L2) + the sample/proto type ([float]→[[float]]) change."
  closes_gap = "H_1198 honest split: its DIM=8 byte-feature growth was a labelled NUMPY MIRROR (cells→~70, 7.4x) because the live AdaptField was 1-D scalar and could not take a DIM>1 sample without an engine change. H_1199 BUILDS that engine change → the DIM=8 leg is now the real .hexa engine (cells→~173, 8.4x). Gap CLOSED; no phantom wiring (DIM>1 nested [[float]] verified to append/index/mutate in hexa before the edit)."
