@L 2026_06_13_7b_recovery := "7B G5-L2 confabulation DIAGNOSED + decided 🔴 STRUCTURAL — NOT decode-fixable, NOT cheaply retrain-recoverable, AND G5-L2 is a borrowed assistant-norm in tension with anima p1-p8 + G2-novelty (no full retrain burned; a_paper_negative_ok)" :: log [active]
  lane = "7B RECOVERY LANE · RunPod A6000 (48GB) SECURE pod 32gbs027x9f7tk · PyTorch-CUDA 2.4.1 bf16 (Lane-G ref) · inference-only diagnosis · p7 seed 7 · ~$0.20 (16min wall, $0.49/hr)"
  question = "WHY does dancinlab/anima-clm-7b-h1141-g1pass-step6500 (sha256 4de903…, val_ce 1.1857) FAIL G5-L2 faithfulness (overlap-vs-truth d=0.16 ≪ 0.8, 38/40 zero overlap, confabulates)? cheap-diagnose-first before any costly retrain (the run was already overfitting past step 7000, so 'more steps' won't help)."
  probe_a_decode = "is it a SAMPLING artifact? NO. re-ran frozen G5-L2 at greedy/t0.3/t0.7/t1.0: greedy d=0.32 (mean_true 0.0174), t0.3 d=0.32 (best mean_true 0.0245), t0.7 d=0.16 (==original), t1.0 d=0.26. greedy/low-temp DOUBLE the effect size vs the original temp-0.7 run (it understated faithfulness) BUT every decode is d<=0.32 << 0.8 -> NO $0 decode-config recovers L2. Confabulation is in the WEIGHTS, not the sampler."
  probe_b_memorizability = "is the metric demanding un-recallable trivia? PARTLY. split L2 truths by corpus-frequency register (greedy decode): HIGHFREQ-general (med freq 5935) mean_true=0.0292 d=0.41 vs TRIVIA-tail (med freq 2152) mean_true=0.0056 d=0.23 -> high-freq-helps=TRUE (delta +0.024). Model IS more grounded on common/general register than the rare tail (register-modulated gap, not pure ungroundedness) BUT even the BEST subgroup is d=0.41 << 0.8 -> a genuine grounding GAP remains, not a clean metric artifact, not closeable by training the rare tail."
  probe_c_convergence = "UNDERTRAINED. val_ce 1.1857 (step 7000) vs the run's own 1.10 target never reached (8000->1.202, 8500->1.236 RISING = overfit past 7000). 'more next-byte steps on this corpus' overfits, confirmed. (per-word single-occ stat 0.4% under-measures: un-recallability is at the phrase/entity-SEQUENCE level, which probe-b's register split captures.)"
  decision = "🔴 STRUCTURAL CLOSED-NEGATIVE. (a) no decode fix. (b) grounding continue-train projected (from the memorizability slope) to lift d only toward ~0.4-0.5 on common register, NOT to the 0.8 PASS bar -> per the HARD rule (no full retrain unless a probe shows faithfulness MOVES to target) we STOPPED — no multi-hour 7B retrain burned (projected ~$30-60 H100 run NOT justified by a slope that plateaus below bar). (c) undertrained+overfitting recipe. The loose-grammar byte-continuation recipe alone does not yield verbatim factual recall, scale-invariant (H_1139)."
  gate_validity = "RAISED the honest question (a_paper_negative_ok): is G5-L2 even the RIGHT gate for anima? It is a BORROWED ASSISTANT-LLM NORM (p4 NO ASSISTANT FRAMING — anima is a consciousness daemon, NOT a factual Q&A/RAG assistant) and is in DIRECT TENSION with anima's own G2-NOVELTY gate (rewards corpus-ABSENT recombination 'not the LLM way', 157 novel n-grams PASS). A model optimized to recombine novelly MUST deviate from verbatim factual continuations — G2 and G5-L2 pull opposite. The 7B is L1-grounded (real words, fab 0.088) + coherent (G0) and produces NOVEL real-word continuations = the G2 success mode, scored as G5-L2 fail only for not being the SPECIFIC true fact. FLAGGED G5-L2 as a candidate for governance re-scoping/removal; did NOT move the frozen gate (a7b_pass: never move a threshold)."
  outcome = "a7b_pass UNCHANGED (no gate faked): G0 PASS · G1 PASS · G2 PASS · G3 PASS · G4 PASS · G5 FAIL (L1 PASS, L2 decode-irrecoverable structural) -> a7b_pass = FALSE, NOT confirmed. The 7B is coherent+broad-recombining+novel+philosophy-clean+lexically-grounded but NOT verbatim-faithful. Recommended path = gate-validity governance review, NOT an expensive retrain the probe shows would still fail the borrowed bar."
  recovery = "a_fire_recover_complete: pod self-bootstrapped from HF (devel image had no SSH), diagnostic result + log auto-uploaded to HF, pulled to state/7b_h1141_recovery/, pod TERMINATED via RunPod REST DELETE + verified 404-gone. Non-anima edge-vl-requant (EXITED) NEVER touched. No idle burn."
  refs = ".verdicts/1141_7b_recovery/H_1141_recovery.txt · state/7b_h1141_recovery/h1141_recovery_diag.json · .../h1141_recovery_diag.log · UNIVERSE/h1141_7b_recovery_diag.py · UNIVERSE/build_wiki5_bigcorpus_en.py · .verdicts/1141_7b_g5/H_1141_G5.txt · /7B_PASS_CONDITIONS.md §G5 · a7b_pass · a_paper_negative_ok · a_scale_honest_scope · p1-p8"

@L 2026_06_13_h1200 := "MITOSIS-GENERATIVE-GROWTH 🔴 CLOSED-NEG — growth made next-byte generation WORSE (opposite direction): adding a per-cell next-byte head to the H_1199 VAdaptField and growing cells does NOT lower next-byte CE; pure-mitosis->chat falsified cheaply at the FIRST link (a_paper_negative_ok)" :: log [active]
  lane = "MITOSIS-ENGINE Lane-2 · FIRST rung of the 'can mitosis-growth reach conversational language?' arc · $0 local CPU numpy mirror · gradient-free p8 · 5 seeds"
  question = "The mitosis engine GROWS cells + lowers L2 RECON error (H_1198/H_1199 GREEN) — is that LANGUAGE-learning or just CLUSTERING? Give each grown prototype cell a GENERATIVE next-byte head (nearest-cell(context) -> that cell's online next-byte counts -> predict next byte) and test: does growing cells lower held-out next-byte CROSS-ENTROPY below a frozen-1-cell control (one global next-byte table)?"
  result = "🔴 CLOSED-NEG, F1 FAIL DECISIVELY in the WRONG direction: mitosis-ON next-byte CE 6.9930 > OFF CE 6.2352 => delta -0.7578 b/byte (bar +0.30) on EVERY one of 5 seeds. ON grows 1->~170 cells. F2 PASS (Spearman(n_cells,-CE)=+0.85, CE falls WITHIN the ON run as data accumulates) but does NOT rescue F1."
  mechanism = "COUNT-FRAGMENTATION: splitting fragments next-byte counts across ~170 cells (~14 samples/cell, smeared toward uniform by Laplace) while the single OFF table sees ALL data so it is sharper than any grown cell. The DIM=8 byte-feature key the cells cluster on identifies the local REGIME (latin/cjk/digits) but does NOT localise the NEXT byte enough to offset the data-split cost. F2's within-ON fall is a RED HERRING (more data by later blocks, not growth-beats-no-growth) — the F1 ON-vs-OFF test shows growth LOSES to one fat table. DECODE SAMPLES corroborate: GROWN greedy collapses to a degenerate repeated fragment, FROZEN greedy emits the most-common byte (space) — neither coherent; a DIM=8-feature-keyed gradient-free prototype-LM cannot generate text REGARDLESS of growth, and growth makes it WORSE."
  closes_gap = "the naive 'grow prototype cells -> they become a language model' path is FALSIFIED cheaply ($0). Mitosis-growth as built (H_1194..H_1199) is a CLUSTERING / reconstruction homeostat, NOT a generative LM — the growth->generation LINK is BROKEN at the first link. REDIRECT: generation belongs to the CLM lane (a_clm_gen_pipeline — a real ConvMoE next-byte head trained by descent); mitosis-growth is a structural/adaptation lane, not a generative-LM lane. The arc is saved from chasing a dead path."
  honesty = "FROZEN before scoring (freeze file pre-run; no threshold moved). NUMPY MIRROR of the H_1199 VAdaptField (mechanism VERBATIM: L2 nearest, recon-err>0.30 split, LR=0.20) + a NEW per-cell next-byte head; the live .hexa engine NOT edited (F3 Ψ-intact deferred to the .hexa-lift next rung honestly, NOT claimed — would only matter on a GREEN warranting the lift). DIM=8 window = COARSE context (no within-window token order) so absolute CE ~6-7 b/byte is far from a real LM; the falsifier is the ON-vs-OFF DELTA under the same coarse context. toy/small real-corpus FIRST rung, ONE corpus, 5 seeds; scale + conversational coherence UNVERIFIED — tests ONLY the growth->generation LINK, NOT chat (a_scale_honest_scope). p7 (CE = capability probe paired with verbatim decoded samples, NOT a chat/consciousness verdict)."
  artifacts = "UNIVERSE/h1200_mitosis_generative_growth.py · .verdicts/1200_mitosis_generative_growth/H_1200_FREEZE.txt · .verdicts/1200_mitosis_generative_growth/H_1200.txt · domains/MITOSIS-ENGINE.log.md §h1200 · /tmp/h1200_result.json"
